msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/module.gd:288
msgid "How opaque the stroke gets. It reaches this and stops, however often the stroke crosses itself."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/module.gd:310
msgid "How sharp the edge of the holes the texture leaves is. Low fades paint in around them and thins the grain towards the stroke's edge."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/module.gd:324
msgid "What the stroke paints through: a grain, streaks along the stroke, or a pattern."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/module.gd:341
msgid "Shifts the texture against the pressure. Above 0 paint needs a firmer press, below 0 a lighter one."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/module.gd:357
msgid "0 paints the same texture and the same random values every stroke. Above 0 each stroke gets its own."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/module.gd:372
msgid "How much paint the stroke lays in height where the texture is light. Nought lays none."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/module.gd:389
msgid "How much more impasto a leaning pen lays on the side it leans to, and less on the other. Below 0 the other side lays more. An upright pen lays it evenly."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/module.gd:398
msgid "Push Colour Below"
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/module.gd:405
msgid "Pushes the colour of the paint on the layers below along with the stroke, as far as that paint stands in height. Off pushes only this layer's paint. The Background and the paper are never pushed."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/module.gd:428
msgid "Colour variation"
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/module.gd:438
msgid "How far the colour's hue and saturation follow the texture under each dab."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/module.gd:480
msgid "How far each dab turns the picked colour's hue, following the sensors."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/module.gd:490
msgid "How Strength follows the sensors. Off by default, because pressure already sets the threshold."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/module.gd:501
msgid "How the Thickness row follows the sensors. Pressure raises it by default, and a pen laid flat or a fast hand lays thinner paint."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/module.gd:513
msgid "How far the pen's lean stretches the tip along it. A pen laid flat paints a tip twice as long by default."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/module.gd:525
msgid "How the Tilt Thickness row follows the sensors. An upright pen lays evenly and one laid flat lays the row's full difference by default."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/module.gd:536
msgid "How the Drift row follows the sensors. A fast stroke carries the texture further by default, so its streaks draw out."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/module.gd:549
msgid "How far the tip is turned, following the sensors. Off by default, so a picture tip keeps its own angle whatever the pen does."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/module.gd:576
msgid "One paints colour only. Two also paints impasto, as much as Thickness lays."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/module.gd:579
msgid "Channels"
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/module.gd:579
msgid "One"
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/module.gd:579
#: ui/settings/look/shape_check_rows.gd:104
msgid "Two"
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/module.gd:585
msgid "How closely the impasto follows the texture's second channel."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/module.gd:588
msgid "Impasto"
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/module.gd:599
msgid "Drift"
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/module.gd:610
msgid "How far the texture slides with the brush. 0 holds it still, 100% drags it so streaks run the whole way."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/noise_brush_settings.gd:731
msgid "The brush's texture '%s' is missing, so it paints with Grain. Put %s back to have it again."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/noise_fields.gd:361
msgid "Bristle"
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/noise_fields.gd:365
#: ui/main/main_dockers.gd:41
#: ui/main/main_dockers.gd:354
#: ui/welcome/welcome_picture.gd:123
msgid "Picture"
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/noise_fields.gd:386
msgid "How wide one speck of the grain is, in pixels of the document."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/noise_fields.gd:397
msgid "How far the grain is stretched about its middle. Low is a soft haze of specks, high a hard pepper."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/noise_fields.gd:406
msgid "Count"
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/noise_fields.gd:410
msgid "How many streaks lie across the stroke."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/noise_fields.gd:422
msgid "How far each streak strays across the stroke from an even comb. 0 lays them evenly."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/noise_fields.gd:435
msgid "How far a streak runs along the stroke before it breaks, in widths of the brush."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/noise_fields.gd:455
msgid "The pattern the stroke paints through, from Sara's patterns or your own."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/noise_fields.gd:468
msgid "How large one repeat of the pattern is, against its own pixels."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/noise_fields.gd:477
msgid "How far the pattern is turned, in degrees."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/noise_fields.gd:490
msgid "Lets the pattern's light parts take paint first. Off, its dark parts take paint at any pressure and its white only at a full press."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/noise_look_rows.gd:30
msgid "How much of the stroke's body paints at a working press whatever the texture says. The texture then shows in the paint's tone and impasto rather than as holes."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/noise_look_rows.gd:34
msgid "Texture Tone"
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/noise_look_rows.gd:36
msgid "How far the texture darkens and lightens the paint, a stop and a half either way at 100%, so it is laid in the colour rather than cut out of it."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/noise_look_rows.gd:40
msgid "Rim Firmness"
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/noise_look_rows.gd:42
msgid "How firm the stroke's edge stays under a soft Hardness. At 0 the edge thins out as Hardness says, at 100% the texture runs whole to the outline."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/noise_look_rows.gd:46
msgid "Build Up"
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/noise_look_rows.gd:47
msgid "How much more paint going back over the stroke's own paint lays there. At 0 a scrub lays no more than its first pass."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/noise_look_rows.gd:54
msgid "Strand Width"
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/noise_look_rows.gd:58
msgid "How wide the bristles' strands are against the width each draws, from 25% at the left end to 300% at the right. At 100% each strand is as wide as it draws, and wider strands merge into a fill."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/noise_look_rows.gd:63
msgid "Strand Softness"
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/noise_look_rows.gd:67
msgid "How soft the strands' edges are drawn, from 0% at the left end, where every strand is as sharp as a strand gets, to 200% at the right, where their edges fade over a third of their width. At 50% each strand draws its own softness, and at 100% half of them are as soft as a strand gets."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/noise_look_rows.gd:72
msgid "Strand Taper"
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/noise_look_rows.gd:73
msgid "How much a strand narrows to a point where its run breaks. At 0 it keeps its width until it fades."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/presets/noise_presets.gd:44
msgid "Sara noise"
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/presets/noise_presets.gd:159
msgid "Grain Round"
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/presets/noise_presets.gd:164
msgid "A round that paints through a fine paper grain, speckled at a light touch and solid at a hard press, for laying in colour with a tooth to it."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/presets/noise_presets.gd:184
msgid "Bristle Flat"
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/presets/noise_presets.gd:189
msgid "Long streaks that drag with the stroke the way a loaded flat's hairs do, broken at a light touch and closing into solid paint at a hard press, for blocking in and for hair and grass."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/presets/noise_presets.gd:214
#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/presets/noise_presets.gd:226
msgid "Canvas Scumble"
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/presets/noise_presets.gd:219
msgid "Paint broken over a woven canvas, the threads taking it and the hollows left open, for scumbling one colour over another."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/presets/noise_presets.gd:236
msgid "Thick Impasto"
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/presets/noise_presets.gd:241
msgid "Paint laid two millimetres thick a stroke, its bristle ridges standing up to catch the light, for the passages that should sit off the canvas."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/presets/noise_presets.gd:259
msgid "Dry Brush"
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/presets/noise_presets.gd:264
msgid "A brush nearly out of paint, skipping over the grain's peaks however hard the press, for scratchy highlights and broken edges."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/presets/noise_presets.gd:285
msgid "Living Colour"
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/presets/noise_presets.gd:290
msgid "Each speck of the grain turns the colour's hue and saturation its own way, so no patch is one flat colour, for skin, foliage and anything alive. A grey has no hue of its own, so on a grey the specks come out a pinkish red."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/presets/noise_presets.gd:305
msgid "Watery Lift"
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/presets/noise_presets.gd:310
msgid "Paint that thins and greys as the pen lets go, like a wet brush lifting off the paper, for glazes that fade out at their ends."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/presets/noise_presets.gd:332
msgid "Broken Chalk"
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/presets/noise_presets.gd:337
msgid "A chalk whose edge a fine paper grain breaks, every stroke meeting the same grain the way chalk meets the tooth of one sheet, for drawing and hatching on a toned ground. It paints in a mixing blend mode where a mixing module is installed, so over another colour it mixes as paint does, blue over yellow turning green."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/presets/noise_presets.gd:376
msgid "Wood Grain"
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/presets/noise_presets.gd:381
msgid "Fine straight streaks at half opacity that run with the stroke, broken at a light touch and filled in between at a hard press, where the streaks stay darker than the paint around them, for the grain of planed wood and any texture that has a direction. A thickness adds a relief, which shows through every layer above it."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/presets/noise_presets.gd:402
msgid "Wet Into Wet"
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/presets/noise_presets.gd:407
msgid "Bristle Flat's streaks loaded with the wet paint they cross, so a stroke opens in its own colour and closes in what it dragged through, for mixing on the canvas alla prima. It paints in a mixing blend mode where a mixing module is installed, so over another colour it mixes as paint does, blue over yellow turning green."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/presets/noise_presets.gd:461
msgid "Firm Fill"
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/presets/noise_presets.gd:466
msgid "A flat, opaque fill with a firm edge, the grain showing in it as light and dark and as relief rather than as holes, in the manner of an impasto flat tip, for laying in shapes that hold."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/presets/noise_presets.gd:485
msgid "Smeary Flat"
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/presets/noise_presets.gd:490
msgid "Wide, soft strands that pick up the paint they cross and push it along, so a stroke smears the colour under it into its own, in the manner of smeary brushes, for blending and for wet passages."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/presets/noise_presets.gd:525
msgid "Sea Sponge"
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/presets/noise_presets.gd:530
msgid "A sponge's open, irregular print that fills in as it is worked over the same place, in the manner of a sponge, for foliage, stone and broken ground."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/presets/noise_presets.gd:548
msgid "Ribbon Pen"
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/presets/noise_presets.gd:553
msgid "A few broad, crisp strands that keep their width to the stroke's end like a ribbon of ink, in the manner of a ribbon pen, for lettering, folds and calligraphic marks."
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/presets/noise_presets.gd:575
msgid "Graphite Pencil"
msgstr ""

#: modules/sara-noise-brush-engine/presets/noise_presets.gd:580
msgid "A fine line in the colour picked that catches the paper's tooth at a light touch and darkens as it is gone over again, in the manner of a pencil, for drawing and hatching."
msgstr ""

