#: ui/settings/look/display_page.gd:256
msgid "What happens to a colour the screen or an 8 or 16-bit file cannot hold, a negative channel above all. Clip cuts each channel on its own, which is what other programs write and can turn the hue. Oklab keeps the lightness and the hue and gives up chroma until the colour fits, and is the default. View > Gamut Mapping switches between the two. Stored pixels, EXR and 32-bit TIFF are never touched."
